\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Sun of my soul, Thou Saviour dear;
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 It is not night if Thou be near
\par O may no earth-born cloud arise
\par  To hid Thee form Thy servant's eyes.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. When the soft dews of kindly sleep
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj My wearied eyelids gently steep;
\par Be my last thought, how sweet to rest
\par For ever on my Saviour's breast
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Abide with me from morn till eve;
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 For without Thee I cannot live;
\par Abide with me when night is nigh
\par For without Thee I dare not die
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  If some poor wandering child of Thine
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Have spurned to-day the voice divine
\par Now, Lord the gracious work begin
\par Let him no more lie down in sin
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.  Watch by the sick, enrich the poor
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 with blessings from Thy boundless store;
\par Be every mourner's sleep to-night
\par Like infant's slumbers, pure and light
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  6.  Come near and bless us when we wake'
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj Ere through the world our way we take
\par Till in the ocean of Thy love
\par \pard     We lose ourselves in heaven above. \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

